# Yasharn, Implacable Earth: "Players can't ... sacrifice nonland permanents to cast spells or activate abilities" (CR 101.2,
# 118.3, 601.2h, 602.2b). Bot1 sacrifices its Black Lotus for mana before Yasharn arrives (the positive control); with
# Yasharn out, its Mishra's Bauble ("{T}, Sacrifice this artifact") can't be activated, while Zuran Orb's "Sacrifice a land"
# still can, with the Forest (20 to 22 life). Bot2 is bound too: its Black Lotus can't be activated, nor can Village Rites
# ("sacrifice a creature") be cast with its Ornithopter there, while Crop Rotation's "sacrifice a land" is paid with its
# Forest. Its Diabolic Edict then makes Bot1 sacrifice Yasharn as it resolves - a sacrifice no cost asks for, which Yasharn
# never stopped (the ruling) - and with Yasharn gone the Lotus is activated and Village Rites cast, the Ornithopter sacrificed.

